motivational-shocks.text:
{{Infobox Booster
| title= {{PAGENAME}}
| image= Motivational Shocks Booster Icon.svg
| description= Allows all Helldivers to recover faster after being slowed by an attack, such as acid. Does not mitigate “area effects,” such as EMS strikes.
| source= [[Polar Patriots Premium Warbond#Page_2|Polar Patriots]] <small>{{Tooltip|P1|Page 1}}</small>
| cost= {{Currency|Medals|15}}
| order=10
}}

'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[Boosters|Booster]] in ''[[Helldivers 2]]''. When equipped, all [[Helldiver]]s are able to recover faster after being slowed by certain attacks. While it does mitigate most attacks that slow down movement, it does not mitigate all of them.

== Description ==
{{PAGENAME}} is a booster that allows for greater recovery when being hit by certain attacks that will slow down a Helldiver for a limited time. When equipped, these attacks will reduce the mobility debuff, allowing Helldivers to regain their mobility and continue moving around without restrain. The Booster is only effective against certain attacks, which can be inflicted by an enemy attack (such as an acid spit), or terrain-related obstacles.

== Procurement ==
The {{PAGENAME}} Booster is unlocked on the 1st page of the [[Polar Patriots Premium Warbond]] for {{Currency|Medals|15}}.

== Known Recovery Times ==
[[Status_Effects#Stun Medium|Stun Medium]] effect from [[G-23 Stun]] and [[CQC-30 Stun Baton]] is reduced by about 2.5 seconds. All other stun effects are reduced by half, with the exception of [[Orbital EMS Strike]] clouds.

The slowed effect from Tremors is reduced by 25%, resulting in the standard 10 second de-buff being reduced to 7.5 seconds. <ref name=":0">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Og4stcl48tE&t=317s</ref>

The slowed effect caused from triggering an [[Ice Plant]] is reduced by 25%, resulting in the standard ~5 second de-buff being reduced to ~3.77 seconds. <ref name=":0" />

== Tactical Information ==

==Issues==
{{Quote|Allows all Helldivers to recover faster after being slowed by an attack, such as acid.}}
:At this time, the {{PAGENAME}} Booster doesn't make you recover faster from the slowed effect caused by acid. Whether you bring the booster or not, the duration of the slow effect is the same. It should be a bug according to AH support team.<ref>''"Thank you for the report. I believe the booster should affect acid slows! I've gone ahead and passed this over to our QA team who can investigate it further."'' — Zendesk Arrowhead support.(2025, March 18).</ref>

