sample-extricator.text:
{{Infobox Booster
|title=Sample Extricator
|image=Sample Extricator Booster Icon.svg
|description=Large enemies now have a chance of dropping Samples on death. Capped at 10 drops per mission.
|source=[[Borderline Justice Premium Warbond#Page 3|Borderline Justice]] <small>{{Tooltip|P3|Page 3}}</small>
|cost={{Currency|Medals|65}}
|order=15
}}

'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[Boosters|Booster]] in ''[[Helldivers 2]]''. When equipped, all Large Enemies will have a chance of dropping [[Sample#Common|Common samples]] upon death. The amount varies, but the amount dropped per mission is capped at 10.

== Procurement ==
The {{PAGENAME}} Booster is unlocked on the 3rd page of the [[Borderline Justice Premium Warbond]] for {{Currency|Medals|65}}.

== Tactical Information ==
* This booster is an [[Effects And Modifiers|effect]] that's active throughout a mission, which allows a Helldiver-squad to obtain more common samples than the maximum spawning number.
*This booster is most useful on [[Evacuate High-Value Assets]], [[Eradicate Terminid Swarm]] and [[Eradicate Automaton Forces]], where the map is small and/or spawns are at known locations. This makes finding the samples relatively easy. It is beneficial if the squad has Helldivers who need to farm them for [[Ship Modules|Super Destroyer upgrades]].
**Evacuate High-Value Assets contain fewer samples than regular missions so extracting with 10 additional samples can double the samples you'll extract with. The samples can often be found in a few minutes by checking the [[Evacuate High-Value Assets#Defense Gate|Defense Gate]] after the mission has been completed. 
**Similarly, both eradication missions for the Terminids and Automaton also contain less samples than a regular mission. Adding 10 can double the number of samples found. Finding them takes a bit more effort, but due to the small map size these can also be found with relative ease.
*This booster does not perform well on lower difficulties where Large Enemies do not spawn at all, or in low quantities.
*In terms of the Galactic War, it is beneficial for [[Major Orders|Sample MOs]], where an increase in their collection is important in progressing it. An additional 10 common samples can mean a three-mission operation can potentially yield the same amount as four* missions. (Depending on the difficulty, the extra amount varies) 

